- Fixed idea.package install: the symlink target was a hardcoded build directory (idea-IU-262.9437.185) that goes stale on every upgrade, since JetBrains names the IDEA tarball's top directory by build number, not by version; the directory is now read from the tarball itself, so /opt/idea always points at what was actually extracted (idea-IU-262.10315.125 for 2026.2.2). The install now also removes the old /opt/idea-IU-* directories and the symlink before extracting, like telegram does, so old builds no longer accumulate. CLion and PyCharm are unaffected, their tarballs use name-version directories.
- Fixed telegram.package install: the tarball carries a top level Telegram/ directory, so the binary ended up at /opt/telegram/Telegram/Telegram; extraction now uses --strip-components=1 and the executable is /opt/telegram/Telegram, matching telegram.profile PATH.
- Updated packages from spider run: selenium 4.48.0, julia 1.12.7, telegram 7.1.5. The selenium and julia values confirm yesterday's spider fixes: version aware sort now reports 4.48.0 instead of the alphabetically last 4.9, and the rc exclusion reports the stable 1.12.7 instead of 1.13.0-rc3.

