* 2026-08-25 Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
- Added jenkinsfile.groovy: a minimal Jenkins declarative pipeline runner that executes a Jenkinsfile locally, without Jenkins. The DSL is implemented with closure delegates (one block class per nesting level, DELEGATE_FIRST), steps are methods of the script base class, and `sleep` is rewritten at compile time because Groovy's own Object.sleep(millis) answers it inside closures before any delegate does.
- Added smi-jenkinsfile and smi-jenkinsfile.cmd wrappers plus the smi-jenkinsfile man page.
- jenkinsfile.groovy: the build environment is seeded from the environment of the calling shell, so PATH = "/opt/setmy.info/bin:$PATH" in an environment block extends the real PATH instead of resolving $PATH to null and losing every command on it.
- jenkinsfile.groovy: sh steps run with sh -xe, so each expanded command is echoed and a multi-line script stops at its first failing line, like Jenkins.

